\begin{remark}[Growing normalized neck length]
\label{rem:chow-ii-appd-growing-neck-length}
\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-ii:page-0390}
\dcref{appD:D.15}
\group{Rotational Neckpinches}

If $L(t)=o(\sqrt{\log(1/(T-t))})$, then for each $\varepsilon>0$ and all
sufficiently late times the flow contains an embedded $\varepsilon$-neck of
normalized length $L(t)$.
\end{remark}

